{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>On that day, one shall take up</b> — a proverb." "<b>And one shall lament</b> — like וגבה ונהה, that which shall be in those days." "<b>ונהיה</b> — like שכר האדם לא נהיה; thus the one who is at that time shall lament a lamentation. And some say: כי נהיה is like חולה, by decree of נחלתי ונהיתי." "<b>נשדנו</b> — nif'al paradigm from doubled-root verbs. And the lamenter says: 'The portion of my people HaShem changes to be for a stranger; how does He change what was mine?' And as we hoped for the Shaddai that He would return our fields to us — then the stranger divides them, for the word יחלק זרה is masculine, corresponding to HaShem. And he said זרה corresponding to HaShem, and he said שדינו corresponding to what he said, וחמדו שדות."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {3 "The second clause of comment [3] is textually difficult; the phrase beginning וכאשר קוינו and the interplay of masculine/feminine forms is rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:45.274314183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}